        "Text": {
          "type": "cexolocstring",
          "value": {
            "0": "*A dwarf stands among the toppled record-stones, pale as lamp-smoke, a torn page clutched in his fist* Stranger — hear me. I am Frár, of Balin's colony. We wrote it in the Book of Mazarbul: twenty plots for our dead, twenty seal-fires to keep them. Nineteen were lit before the drums came up from the deep. The twentieth never was — and what lies beneath it does not lie still. Light the three seal-braziers — one in this chamber, two in Balin's Tomb — and face what rises. Do this, and the warden's seal is yours."
          }
        }
      },
      {
